# 低频词汇 List05
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List05核心词汇

errand /ˈerənd/ n. 差事 She sent him on an errand to the post office. 她派他去邮局办事。
espionage /ˈespiənɑːʒ/ n. 间谍活动 He was convicted of industrial espionage. 他被判犯有工业间谍罪。
esteem /ɪˈstiːm/ n./v. 尊重 The professor is held in high esteem by colleagues. 这位教授深受同事尊重。
evacuate /ɪˈvækjueɪt/ v. 疏散 Residents were evacuated before the hurricane. 飓风来临前居民被疏散了。
evoke /ɪˈvəʊk/ v. 唤起 The song evokes memories of childhood. 这首歌唤起了童年的记忆。
exempt /ɪɡˈzempt/ v./adj. 免除 Small businesses are exempt from the new tax. 小企业免征新税。
exile /ˈeksaɪl/ n./v. 流亡 The dissident was forced into exile. 异见人士被迫流亡海外。
exotic /ɪɡˈzɒtɪk/ adj. 奇异的 The market offers exotic fruits from around the world. 该市场提供来自世界各地的奇异水果。
expenditure /ɪkˈspendɪtʃə(r)/ n. 支出 Military expenditure has increased dramatically. 军事支出大幅增加。
expire /ɪkˈspaɪə(r)/ v. 过期 The contract expires at the end of the month. 合同月底到期。
extinct /ɪkˈstɪŋkt/ adj. 灭绝的 Conservation efforts aim to prevent species from going extinct. 保护工作旨在防止物种灭绝。
faction /ˈfækʃn/ n. 派系 The political party split into rival factions. 该政党分裂成了对立的派系。
feat /fiːt/ n. 壮举 The construction of the dam was an engineering feat. 大坝的建造是一项工程壮举。
fervent /ˈfɜːvənt/ adj. 热烈的 She is a fervent believer in education reform. 她是教育改革的热烈信奉者。
flaw /flɔː/ n. 缺陷 The argument has a fundamental flaw. 该论点有一个根本性缺陷。
flee /fliː/ v. 逃离 Thousands of refugees fled the conflict zone. 数千名难民逃离了冲突地区。
fluctuate /ˈflʌktʃueɪt/ v. 波动 Currency exchange rates fluctuate constantly. 货币汇率不断波动。
forge /fɔːdʒ/ v. 锻造 The two nations forged a lasting peace agreement. 两国缔结了一项持久的和平协议。
franchise /ˈfræntʃaɪz/ n. 特许经营 He invested in a restaurant franchise. 他投资了一家餐厅特许经营权。
frantic /ˈfræntɪk/ adj. 疯狂的 There was a frantic search for survivors. 人们疯狂地搜寻幸存者。
fraud /frɔːd/ n. 欺诈 The company was fined for accounting fraud. 该公司因会计欺诈被罚款。
fringe /frɪndʒ/ n./adj. 边缘 The idea was once considered fringe science. 这个想法曾被认为是边缘科学。
futile /ˈfjuːtaɪl/ adj. 徒劳的 Attempts to negotiate proved futile. 谈判的尝试被证明是徒劳的。
garrison /ˈɡærɪsn/ n./v. 驻军 The fort was garrisoned by 500 soldiers. 该堡垒有500名士兵驻守。
genocide /ˈdʒenəsaɪd/ n. 种族灭绝 The world must act to prevent genocide. 世界必须采取行动防止种族灭绝。
glamour /ˈɡlæmə(r)/ n. 魅力 The glamour of the entertainment industry attracts many. 娱乐业的魅力吸引了许多人。
glimpse /ɡlɪmps/ n./v. 一瞥 The report offers a glimpse into the future of technology. 该报告让人一窥技术的未来。
gratitude /ˈɡrætɪtjuːd/ n. 感激 She expressed her gratitude for the generous donation. 她对慷慨捐赠表示感激。
grieve /ɡriːv/ v. 悲伤 The nation grieved the loss of its leader. 全国为失去领导人而悲伤。
grim /ɡrɪm/ adj. 严峻的 The employment situation remains grim. 就业形势依然严峻。
